      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-306163",
      ":question/problem": "The table below shows the weekly sales (in units) for five stores.\n\n| Store | Sales |\n| --- | ---: |\n| A | $210$ |\n| B | $225$ |\n| C | $218$ |\n| D | $230$ |\n| E | $220$ |\n\nA sixth store recorded $240$ sales, and this value is added to the original dataset of five stores to create a new dataset. Complete the following statement so that it correctly compares the means of the two datasets.\n\nThe mean of the original dataset is\n{{field-1}}\nthe mean of the new dataset because the new value is\n{{field-2}}\nthe mean of the original dataset."
    }
